# First-party SHACL Rules case: an ILL-FORMED triple is skipped, not an error.
# SHACL 1.2 Inference Rules, "Execution of triple rules": "For each combination of
# members s of S, p of P and o of O, infer a triple with subject s, predicate p and
# object o. Skip ill-formed triples, for example when a blank node is used as
# predicate." The subject expression here yields a literal and an IRI: the literal
# combination is ill-formed and skipped, the IRI combination is inferred.

@prefix ex:  <http://example.org/ns#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix sh:  <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .

ex:alice rdf:type ex:Person .

ex:BadRule
  rdf:type sh:NodeShape ;
  sh:targetClass ex:Person ;
  sh:rule [
      rdf:type sh:TripleRule ;
      sh:subject ( "notasubject" ex:alice ) ;
      sh:predicate ex:p ;
      sh:object ex:o ] .
